    "game_plan": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "s_roast": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/centenarian-salad-okinawan-sweet-potato-chickpeas.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 0",
            "heading": "Roast the sweet potatoes and chickpeas",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Heat the oven to 425&deg;F and line a sheet pan with parchment. Toss two Okinawan sweet potatoes, cut into &frac12;-inch cubes, with a drained jar of chickpeas, 2 Tbsp olive oil and salt. Spread it out and roast <strong>30 minutes</strong>, until the chickpeas are crisp and the potato is browned.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_eggs": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/centenarian-salad-jammy-egg.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 5",
            "heading": "Soft boil the eggs",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Bring a small pot to a boil, lower in four pasture-raised eggs and boil exactly <strong>7 minutes</strong>. Move them to cold water and leave them 15 minutes before peeling. You want the yolks jammy, not chalky &mdash; that soft centre is where the choline is.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_cold": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/centenarian-salad-honeyed-dill-tzatziki.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 10",
            "heading": "Tzatziki, then the cucumber salad",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Stir together the Greek yogurt, a whole bunch of minced dill, two minced garlic cloves, the juice of a lemon, 2 Tbsp olive oil, 1 Tbsp raw honey and &frac12; tsp salt; refrigerate. Then chop the cherry tomatoes and cucumber, thinly slice the red onion, toss with olive oil and salt, and refrigerate that too.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_salmon": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/centenarian-salad-salmon-lemon-pre-bake.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 30",
            "heading": "Swap in the salmon",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Move the roasted vegetables to a bowl and drop the oven to <strong>350&deg;F</strong>. Onto the same pan: the salmon, patted dry, drizzled with olive oil, salted, with a couple of thin lemon rounds laid on each fillet. Bake <strong>15 minutes</strong>, until just cooked through, then squeeze over the remaining lemon.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_base": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/centenarian-salad-arugula-chickpea-kraut-base.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 45",
            "heading": "Build the base",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Spread two large handfuls of wild arugula across a big platter, then scatter over the roasted sweet potato and chickpeas. Add the purple sauerkraut, kalamata olives and wild blueberries.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_finish": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/centenarian-salmon-salad-finished-platter.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 50",
            "heading": "Finish and sit down",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Add the cucumber-tomato salad, tuck in the avocado slices and broccoli sprouts, set the halved eggs cut side up and lay the salmon on top. Spoon over the tzatziki. Then do the most centenarian thing of all &mdash; sit down with someone and eat slowly.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "s_roast",
        "s_eggs",
        "s_cold",
        "s_salmon",
        "s_base",
        "s_finish"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.timeline.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "image_ratio": "landscape",
        "image_ratio_mobile": "landscape",
        "padding_top": 56,
