    "rich_text_standard": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "h_std": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Salmon clean enough to eat on repeat",
            "heading_size": "title-sm",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "t_std": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A longevity plate falls apart if the protein on it carries a contaminant load. The Mt. Cook Alpine King Salmon here is raised in glacial water in New Zealand&rsquo;s Southern Alps and third-party lab tested: mercury at <strong>0.033 ppm</strong>, inside the 0.1 ppm ceiling of the Seatopia Standard, and <strong>no detectable microplastics</strong> across all six polymers screened.</p><p>Each 7 oz portion delivers roughly <strong>2,300 mg of marine omega-3s</strong> (EPA + DHA) and about 39 g of protein. Any Seatopia salmon works in this recipe &mdash; they all clear the same testing. You can read exactly how we test on our <a href=\"/pages/seatopia-testing-commitment\" title=\"Seatopia's Testing Commitment\">testing commitment page</a>.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
